special_abilities:
  - name: "Major Pact"
    description: "A mortal Soulmancer must make a Major Pact with a Lord of Hell or a dark god of Hell, death or dark magic to learn the craft. After proving his worth through dirty work for a demonic master, he is granted the Gift of Knowledge of Soulmancy and studies for 4D6+12 months before becoming a level one Soulmancer. At graduation he must dispose of the rejected apprentices. He remains beholden to that master for eternity."
  - name: "Minor Supernatural Being"
    description: "The pact transforms the Soulmancer into a minor supernatural being: +1D6x10 Hit Points and +1D6x100 S.D.C. (both in the class bonuses), enough to survive a limited amount of Mega-Damage (generally 1-7 M.D.). A Mega-Damage being who becomes a Soulmancer gains an additional 6D6 M.D.C. instead; that conditional figure is not added by the sheet."
  - name: "Soul Guard"
    description: "Impervious to blood sacrifice (his P.P.E. cannot be drained and used by others) and to Soul Drinking by any means, be it a Rune Weapon, a demonic being, a supernatural creature, magic or another Soulmancer. The save is automatic. Also resistant to possession and mind control (see the O.C.C. bonuses)."
  - name: "Bio-Regeneration"
    description: "Recovers a number of points per day equal to his P.E. attribute, first to Hit Points and then to S.D.C. (or M.D.C. if a Mega-Damage being). Wounds heal overnight but leave numerous scars."
  - name: "Spell Limitations"
    description: "A spell cast as an invocation (rather than during a ritual to create an item) is cast at half the Soulmancer''s current level of experience, and all its features (damage, range, duration and the like) are further reduced by half. P.P.E. cost is unchanged."
  - name: "Blood Cauldron"
    description: "A ritual to gain spell invocations temporarily. Components: a small cauldron, six pints of fresh humanoid blood, an owl''s feather and the brain of an incantation-using spell caster or creature of magic (not a Mystic, Warlock or a being whose spells are imparted). The brain is eaten and the blood drunk, leaving the mage in a Blood Trance for 2D6 hours. He chooses two spells per his level of experience (three from a dragon or similar creature of magic) and keeps them for days equal to his I.Q.; they are cast at half power and cannot be transcribed. Base chance of success: 44% +4% per level of experience; a failure uses up the components, and he may try again after 24 hours."
  - name: "Construct Soulmancy Items and Weapons"
    description: "Skilled at constructing weapons and items and empowering them with Soulmancy. Base skill 60% +3% per level of experience. The book leaves the creation rules out on purpose, because the class is meant for N.P.C.s; most items need living sacrifices and organs as components, which the process consumes."
  - name: "Insanity"
    description: "Every Soulmancer is sadistic, cruel and cold-hearted. Roll on the Psychosis Table (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.334) to determine the specific mental state; the roll is made by hand and not stored here."
