restrictions:
  - "The book presents this O.C.C. as a Non-Player Character, not intended as a player character but as an N.P.C. villain and servant of evil. It is imported by Nate''s ruling of 2026-11-17 so a Game Master can build one; player use is at the Game Master''s discretion."
  - "Alignment: evil only. Aberrant (15%), Miscreant (35%) and Diabolic (50%)."
  - "Races are limited to those who can become spell casters."
  - "Cybernetics: none to start, and avoided at all costs because they interfere with magic and Bio-Regeneration."
  - "+1 to Spell Strength at levels 4, 9 and 15, not modeled. The +2 save vs mind control also covers mind-controlling drugs."
  - "Also starts with 4D6x1,000 credits'' worth of components and Black Market goods, over and above the coin in starting_money, a lesser magical knife, 4 Soul Crystals, a small metal cauldron, a workshop (a torture chamber or lair) and 1D6 mortal slaves who serve as servants, valets or henchmen. At 7th level the master grants one minor supernatural minion (a Lesser Demon or Deevil, or a Sub-Demon or Host of choice), and two more or one greater minion at levels 10 and 15."
extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames printed 85-88 (cache p086-p089, page_offset 1); stats and the Experience Table read off renders of cache 87-89. The section opens with rules for Greater Demons and Deevils learning Soulmancy (printed 85), which are not this class and are not stored. The book heads the class ''A Non-Player Character O.C.C.'' and its stats note says it is not intended as a player character; it is imported as an ordinary published class by Nate''s ruling of 2026-11-17, with the warning carried as the first restriction and the evil tag. occ_group magic and men_of_arms false: the section is headed ''Soulmancer O.C.C. Magic Powers'' and the class is a spell caster, not a Man of Arms. Spells: the nine starting spells are stored by their catalog names. The class page prints ''Create Soul Crystal (Ritual; 30)'' (catalog: Create Soulmancy Soul Crystal, 40 P.P.E.), ''Consume Soul (35)'' (catalog 50), ''Pseudo Life (1 life essence)'' (catalog Pseudo Life (Ritual)) and ''Read Soul (30)'', stored as Read Soul in Object, the one Soulmancy spell whose name and 30 P.P.E. cost match; the catalog costs are the spell section''s own and are not changed here. Soulmancy picks draw from a named list of the 52 Soulmancy spells that are not Spells of Legend (Create Hell Pit, Summon Demon Planet and Youthful Soul are left out, as the book reserves them as boons from the master). spell_traditions_allowed is deliberately not stated: every Soulmancy pick is a named list, so the level-gated conventional picks reach general invocations only, which is exactly what the page grants. Experience Table printed 88. Base P.P.E. printed in ability 6. Literacy: Demongogian has no catalog row and is a Literacy: Other pick with its bonus. Espionage ''Forgery and Wilderness Survival only (+10%)'': Wilderness Survival is filed under Wilderness, which the class also grants, so it is reachable both ways. Pilot ''Robots, Power Armor or Military vehicles'' excluded by name. Equipment without a catalog row (Soul Crystal, lesser magical knife, cauldron, ice pick, saw) is recorded in restrictions and notes, not stubbed; the silk robe is the Robe row and the surgery tools the Surgical Kit. The 6D6 M.D.C. for a Mega-Damage being and Spell Strength are prose."
---

## Lore

Soulmancy, also called Blood Magic or Demon Magic, draws on the life essence of living victims, usually through rituals that end in blood sacrifice. Once the preserve of demons and Deevils, it is now being taught to mortals as the Minion War demands more practitioners: Soulmancers make the weapons and magic items both sides depend on, and without them the Hell Pits cannot be created or activated.

A mortal learns the art only by a Major Pact with a Lord of Hell or a dark god, serving a demonic master through years of dirty work and apprenticeship. On Rifts Earth a Soulmancer advises and serves the Hell Lord or Greater Demon he is assigned to, as a court advisor, high priest, spy or captain, and is always hunting for victims and exotic components for his work. Every Soulmancer is evil, scarred by his own rituals, and usually attended by slaves and supernatural minions.

## GM Notes

The book presents the Soulmancer as an N.P.C. villain, and leaves the rules for building Soulmancy items to the Game Master, using the Soulmancy and bone weapons in the book as a guide.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'soulmancer');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'soulmancer';

